WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.562
This comparison makes NULL policy very concrete With
ordinary not-equal a NULL

00:00:05.588 --> 00:00:10.275
payment status does not produce true It produces
UNKNOWN so the row

00:00:10.288 --> 00:00:15.862
is removed by WHERE IS DISTINCT FROM returns a
definite answer A

00:00:15.875 --> 00:00:18.988
NULL status is distinct from the text Paid so that
row is

00:00:19.012 --> 00:00:24.638
included Neither rule is universally correct The
right choice depends

00:00:24.662 --> 00:00:28.312
on the question If you want only known statuses that
are not

00:00:28.338 --> 00:00:32.850
Paid ordinary inequality may match the rule If you
want everything that

00:00:32.862 --> 00:00:37.350
is not definitely Paid including missing status for
review IS DISTINCT FROM

00:00:37.375 --> 00:00:41.262
is better Run both statements and compare the row
counts
